WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:00.834
You want to talk about

00:00:00.834 --> 00:00:02.469
what the former president is doing,

00:00:02.469 --> 00:00:03.203
both on the legal side

00:00:03.203 --> 00:00:04.604
and also the political side.

00:00:04.604 --> 00:00:05.872
And so both of those, we want to bring in

00:00:05.872 --> 00:00:07.841
CNN reporter Daniel Dale to fact check

00:00:07.841 --> 00:00:09.275
some of the claims made by the former

00:00:09.275 --> 00:00:10.410
president last night

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:12.445
when addressing the crowd at Bedminster.

00:00:12.445 --> 00:00:13.713
Daniel Trump claimed

00:00:13.713 --> 00:00:14.881
that the Espionage Act

00:00:14.881 --> 00:00:16.449
shouldn't be applied in this case.

00:00:16.449 --> 00:00:17.283
Take a listen.

00:00:19.152 --> 00:00:21.087
Charging a former president

00:00:21.087 --> 00:00:22.222
of the United States

00:00:22.222 --> 00:00:26.493
under the Espionage Act of 1917

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:30.630
wasn't meant for this The Espionage Act

00:00:31.264 --> 00:00:33.266
has been used to go after traitors

00:00:33.266 --> 00:00:34.034
and spies.

00:00:34.034 --> 00:00:35.101
It has nothing to do

00:00:35.101 --> 00:00:37.003
with a former president legally

00:00:37.003 --> 00:00:40.306
keeping his own documents

00:00:40.974 --> 00:00:41.474
All right, Daniel,

00:00:41.474 --> 00:00:42.042
there's the

00:00:42.042 --> 00:00:43.276
former president's contention.

00:00:43.276 --> 00:00:44.611
What are the facts?

00:00:44.744 --> 00:00:46.746
So two big problems of fact here.

00:00:46.746 --> 00:00:47.247
First of all,

00:00:47.247 --> 00:00:49.082
these are not his own documents.

00:00:49.082 --> 00:00:50.350
They are the legal property

00:00:50.350 --> 00:00:51.551
of the federal government.

00:00:51.551 --> 00:00:52.485
Second of all, though,

00:00:52.485 --> 00:00:53.953
this idea that the Espionage Act

00:00:53.953 --> 00:00:55.188
is only meant for traitors

00:00:55.188 --> 00:00:57.090
and spies is just not true.

00:00:57.090 --> 00:00:57.424
Of course,

00:00:57.424 --> 00:00:58.958
there are provisions of the Espionage Act

00:00:58.958 --> 00:01:00.460
that target traitors and spies,

00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:00.827
but there's

00:01:00.827 --> 00:01:02.429
also the provision under which Trump

00:01:02.429 --> 00:01:03.063
and many people

00:01:03.063 --> 00:01:04.564
before him have been charged.

00:01:04.564 --> 00:01:06.699
It's known as seven 93.

00:01:06.699 --> 00:01:07.734
And it makes it a crime

00:01:07.734 --> 00:01:09.202
to willfully retain

00:01:09.202 --> 00:01:10.737
national defense information

00:01:10.737 --> 00:01:11.337
and refuse

00:01:11.337 --> 00:01:13.073
to deliver it to the United States.

00:01:13.073 --> 00:01:14.074
Nothing in that provision

00:01:14.074 --> 00:01:15.475
requires you to be a spy

00:01:15.475 --> 00:01:17.243
to to do any classic espionage,

00:01:17.243 --> 00:01:18.578
to even deliver the information

00:01:18.578 --> 00:01:19.212
to anyone.

00:01:19.212 --> 00:01:20.313
And as an example,

00:01:20.313 --> 00:01:20.880
you can go back

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:22.182
and look at another indictment,

00:01:22.182 --> 00:01:23.883
the 2017 indictment

00:01:23.883 --> 00:01:25.685
of a former NSA contractor

00:01:25.685 --> 00:01:26.853
named Harold Martin.

00:01:26.853 --> 00:01:28.555
He was accused of taking a whole bunch

00:01:28.555 --> 00:01:29.823
of classified information

00:01:29.823 --> 00:01:31.558
and just keeping it in his car

00:01:31.558 --> 00:01:32.325
and his house.

00:01:32.325 --> 00:01:33.693
He was never accused in court

00:01:33.693 --> 00:01:35.862
of giving it to anyone of being a spy.

00:01:35.895 --> 00:01:36.996
He was essentially portrayed

00:01:36.996 --> 00:01:38.164
as a kind of hoarder.

00:01:38.164 --> 00:01:39.666
He ended up pleaded guilty.

00:01:39.666 --> 00:01:40.767
So not a spy.

00:01:40.767 --> 00:01:41.835
This provision was applied

00:01:41.835 --> 00:01:44.003
and he was convicted and sentenced.

00:01:44.003 --> 00:01:45.171
One other thing

00:01:45.171 --> 00:01:46.206
that's so interesting

00:01:46.206 --> 00:01:47.941
is that the former president

00:01:47.941 --> 00:01:48.641
made the point

00:01:48.641 --> 00:01:50.443
that instead of the Espionage Act,

00:01:50.443 --> 00:01:51.778
the law that should be applied

00:01:51.778 --> 00:01:54.180
here is the Presidential Records Act,

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:55.081
which actually isn't

00:01:55.081 --> 00:01:56.683
part of the indictment. Listen to this.

00:01:58.585 --> 00:01:59.185
Threatening

00:01:59.185 --> 00:02:01.754
me with 400 years in prison

00:02:02.188 --> 00:02:03.623
for possessing my own

00:02:03.623 --> 00:02:04.958
presidential papers,

00:02:04.958 --> 00:02:06.426
which just about every other

00:02:06.426 --> 00:02:08.061
president has done

00:02:08.061 --> 00:02:10.730
is one of the most outrageous and vicious

00:02:10.730 --> 00:02:11.464
legal theories

00:02:11.464 --> 00:02:12.532
ever put forward

00:02:12.532 --> 00:02:15.335
in an American court of law.

00:02:15.335 --> 00:02:17.604
As president the law that applies to

00:02:17.604 --> 00:02:21.241
this case is not the Espionage Act,

00:02:21.374 --> 00:02:22.442
but very simply,

00:02:22.442 --> 00:02:24.577
the Presidential Records Act,

00:02:25.245 --> 00:02:26.746
which is not even mentioned

00:02:26.746 --> 00:02:30.250
in this ridiculous 44 page indictment

00:02:31.017 --> 00:02:33.153
under the Presidential Records Act,

00:02:33.153 --> 00:02:35.855
which is civil, not criminal.

00:02:35.855 --> 00:02:36.789
I had every right

00:02:36.789 --> 00:02:39.626
to have these documents.

00:02:39.792 --> 00:02:41.461
Putting aside the fact

00:02:41.461 --> 00:02:43.096
that that's not even in the indictment,

00:02:43.096 --> 00:02:44.564
if it were.

00:02:44.564 --> 00:02:45.732
Does that does appear

00:02:45.732 --> 00:02:47.700
absolve him of any of this?

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:48.568
It it does.

00:02:48.568 --> 00:02:49.035
And the idea

00:02:49.035 --> 00:02:50.170
that the Presidential Records

00:02:50.170 --> 00:02:51.871
Act absolves former

00:02:51.871 --> 00:02:54.140
President Trump here is like upside down

00:02:54.140 --> 00:02:55.642
bizarro world stuff.

00:02:55.642 --> 00:02:57.544
That law, Poppy, is unequivocal.

00:02:57.544 --> 00:02:59.445
It says that all official records

00:02:59.445 --> 00:03:00.513
from a presidency

00:03:00.513 --> 00:03:01.481
are the property

00:03:01.481 --> 00:03:02.282
of the federal government,

00:03:02.282 --> 00:03:03.383
the National Archives.

00:03:03.383 --> 00:03:04.117
The moment

00:03:04.117 --> 00:03:05.718
that President leaves office,

00:03:05.718 --> 00:03:06.319
as one expert

00:03:06.319 --> 00:03:06.920
put it to me,

00:03:06.920 --> 00:03:08.621
the fact that former President Trump

00:03:08.621 --> 00:03:10.323
violated the Presidential Records Act

00:03:10.323 --> 00:03:11.958
does not prevent him from being charged

00:03:11.958 --> 00:03:13.927
for also allegedly violating

00:03:13.927 --> 00:03:14.627
another law

00:03:14.627 --> 00:03:15.061
And I'll add,

00:03:15.061 --> 00:03:16.462
there's two other problems of fact

00:03:16.462 --> 00:03:17.730
in that quote we just played.

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:18.364
Number one, he's

00:03:18.364 --> 00:03:19.399
not actually being threatened

00:03:19.399 --> 00:03:20.733
with 400 years in prison.

00:03:20.733 --> 00:03:21.601
Federal sentencing

00:03:21.601 --> 00:03:23.603
does not work by adding up the maximum

00:03:23.603 --> 00:03:25.371
possible sentence for each crime.

00:03:25.371 --> 00:03:26.773
So that's not realistic.

00:03:26.773 --> 00:03:27.507
And second of all,

00:03:27.507 --> 00:03:28.341
it's just not true

00:03:28.341 --> 00:03:30.243
that just about every other president

00:03:30.243 --> 00:03:31.411
has done what he's done.

00:03:31.411 --> 00:03:32.478
No other president

00:03:32.478 --> 00:03:34.147
in the Presidential Records Act era

00:03:34.147 --> 00:03:35.215
So starting with President

00:03:35.215 --> 00:03:37.116
Ronald Reagan has done anything like

00:03:37.116 --> 00:03:38.818
take a trove of sensitive

00:03:38.818 --> 00:03:40.587
classified documents and refuse

00:03:40.587 --> 00:03:41.221
to give them back

00:03:41.221 --> 00:03:42.155
to the federal government.

00:03:42.155 --> 00:03:44.224
When asked repeatedly to do so

00:03:44.224 --> 00:03:45.158
right there

00:03:45.158 --> 00:03:48.228
in the willful retention allegation.

00:03:48.228 --> 00:03:49.162
Daniel Dale, thank you.

00:03:49.162 --> 00:03:50.530
Your fact checks are gold.

00:03:50.530 --> 00:03:51.331
We appreciate them.

